{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/6639-wild-west-game","id":6639,"title":"Wild West Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-08T22:36:47-08:00","id":6639,"title":"Wild West Game","content":"So I want to run a game set in the expanding frontier of post civil America. What sort of sources should I draw from for inspiration, be they folktales, film, literature, etc? Are there any official books set in the wild west to check out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/943-chewbaklava","name":"chewbaklava","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T22:43:51-08:00","id":6642,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: The Wild West springs to mind. If you can find it the original western game Boot Hill maybe useful. For story ideas go watch a bunch of John Ford Westerns and of course John Wayne movies that Ford did not direct. I'd start with Rooster Cogburn both of them and then perhaps a few Eastwood films. I have a special fondness for Big Jake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T00:15:27-08:00","id":6673,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: The Wild West is of course the one most useful for WoD games, and regular westerns are good idea sources too, but do not forget some of the other supernatural or otherwise weird western sources. The game Deadlands (especially its scenario books) might work though it is possibly too far out. True Blood has some old west flashbacks. There are movies like \u201cThe Strangers Gundown\u201d, \u201cThe Living Coffin\u201d, \u201cCurse of the Undead\u201d, \u201cThe Beast of Hollow Mountain\u201d, \u201cBlack Noon\u201d, \u201cThe Curse of Demon Mountain\u201d and others too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T06:47:27-08:00","id":6788,"title":"","content":"Try and find a novel that came out a few years back, called &quot;The Half-Made World.&quot; It's a vaguely historical New Weird/Wild West story about the conflict between The Line (a bureaucratic society that treats people as cogs and worships the railroads as Lovecraftian gods) and The Gun (a loosely-associated group of gunslingers who sold their souls in order to become superhumanly talented with a revolver). It's a fantastic read, and The Line is the perfect example of what a more overt God-Machine would look like during the Wild West.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T07:57:11-08:00","id":6829,"title":"","content":"Oh man you've just reminded me the Supernatural 1st season cap where they discover the gun that Colt made for a hunter in the wild west... That setting could be great for hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/828-j7hunter","name":"j7hunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}